From 9eeabb599206cbf23e852367fa267977621e740c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emma Anholt <anholt@igalia.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:43:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] drm/msm: make register usage header generation
 deterministic

The register generator iterates a Python set when collecting per-variant
usage arrays. Hash seeds therefore change the generated declaration
order and, through header checksums in debug data, reproducible object
and module outputs.

Backport Emma Anholt's Mesa c09c414563fc change by sorting variants
before collecting usage arrays. Preserve each array key/register pair
and every non-usage declaration.

On this pinned msm-fixes source, five seeds produce three baseline
headers and one fixed header. All 18 usage arrays and other declarations
are preserved. Both native complete MSM components build with the
fixed generator, W=1 and no compiler diagnostics.

The original Mesa change was marked Generated-by: LLM. Codex (GPT-6)
assisted the earlier Linux draft and this source-base qualification.
Full package reproducibility and physical acceptance remain separate.

Fixes: 5acf49119630 ("drm/msm: import gen_header.py script from Mesa")
Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/commit/c09c414563fc0fe6788f28ee7a35522ab21d0ed5
Assisted-by: LLM

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/registers/gen_header.py b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/registers/gen_header.py
index d3b56a9d84fb..5a738a2ad173 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/registers/gen_header.py
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/registers/gen_header.py
@@ -816,7 +816,7 @@ class Parser(object):
                         if reg == vreg:
                             d[(usage, sanitize_variant(variant))].append(reg)
                 else:
-                    for variant in self.variants:
+                    for variant in sorted(self.variants):
                         d[(usage, sanitize_variant(variant))].append(reg)
 
         print("#ifdef __cplusplus")
